              "text": "diàochá is built from diào 'to choose' and chá, both inherited from Middle Chinese, dewH and dzrae (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'to select' and the second 'wood floating in water'; how the pair came to mean 'to investigate' is not settled."
